{
  "version": 1,
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "public-prefix-then-tenant",
      "kind": "composition",
      "draft_test": 1,
      "fragments": [
        {
          "id": "tools",
          "constraints": {
            "retention": {
              "mode": "allow",
              "max_age": 86400
            },
            "reuse": "exact",
            "share_max": "public",
            "namespace": "tools:v7"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "system",
          "constraints": {
            "retention": {
              "mode": "allow",
              "max_age": 3600
            },
            "reuse": "exact",
            "share_max": "tenant",
            "namespace": "agent:v4"
          }
        }
      ],
      "expected": {
        "after_fragment_0": {
          "retention": {
            "mode": "allow",
            "max_age": 86400
          },
          "reuse": "exact",
          "share_max": "public",
          "namespace_identity": "b42d2c88b53bb913c2637817ff163308807ac7ba31ecf20bca0631fabccd38e1"
        },
        "after_fragment_1": {
          "retention": {
            "mode": "allow",
            "max_age": 3600
          },
          "reuse": "exact",
          "share_max": "tenant",
          "namespace_identity": "747083201bfe64956b7607c3202ad0a21214b11de2404d188f30455d4f773dcc"
        }
      },
      "comment": "Also pins which fragments the effective namespace digest ranges over. after_fragment_0 covers state that depends on the tools fragment alone, so it digests one namespace. Reading the construction as ranging over every fragment in the request gives the two-namespace digest instead, and the two implementations then share nothing on this prefix."
    },
